> [12.3.1](https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/blob/v4.0.3/4.0/en/0x20-V12-Files-Resources.md#v123-file-execution) Verify that user-submitted filename metadata is not used directly by system or framework filesystems and that a URL API is used to protect against path traversal.

From the requirement, it is not clear what exactly is meant by "URL API" and how do I use it to protect against path traversal. If I go with common Java check for path traversal, is `File` class the "URL API" here?

```
File file = new File(BASE_DIRECTORY, userInput);
if (file.getCanonicalPath().startsWith(BASE_DIRECTORY)) {
    // process file
}
```

Searching cheat sheets and Google for URL API references, I got nothing but [URL Web API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/URL) - not sure how would I use that for path traversal protection (maybe in Node.js?).
